{"id":"8af8810b5026b75f","group":"93","path":"93/93-ax-tarski.md","title":"Tarski","display":"ax-tarski — Tarski","type":"axiom","metadata":{"type":"axiom","book":"Algebraizable Logics","book_abbrev":"93","label":"93-ax-tarski","aliases":["93-ax-tarski"],"display":"ax-tarski — Tarski","depends_on":["[[93-df-consequence]]","[[93-df-logic]]","[[93-df-language]]","[[93-df-formula]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"axiom"},{"key":"book","html":"Algebraizable Logics"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"93"},{"key":"label","html":"93-ax-tarski"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>93-ax-tarski</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"ax-tarski — Tarski"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"afd7605d365be7b6\" href=\"?note=afd7605d365be7b6\" title=\"93-df-consequence\">93-df-consequence</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bd7e4207897c8db3\" href=\"?note=bd7e4207897c8db3\" title=\"93-df-logic\">93-df-logic</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"a33dcee0f62c9026\" href=\"?note=a33dcee0f62c9026\" title=\"93-df-language\">93-df-language</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"c2ca1af9af149e69\" href=\"?note=c2ca1af9af149e69\" title=\"93-df-formula\">93-df-formula</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F\">\\(F\\)</span> is a formula carrier, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\tau\">\\(\\tau\\)</span> is its connective type, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash)\">\\(\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash)\\)</span> is the type-indexed logic predicate of <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"bd7e4207897c8db3\" href=\"?note=bd7e4207897c8db3\" title=\"93-df-logic\">93-df-logic</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Gamma,\\Delta\\subseteq F\">\\(\\Gamma,\\Delta\\subseteq F\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\\in F\">\\(\\varphi\\in F\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}tarski}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash)\\to\\Bigl[{}&amp;\n\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\Gamma\\;(\\Gamma\\vdash\\varphi)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq\\Delta\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\n(\\Gamma\\vdash\\varphi\\to\\Delta\\vdash\\varphi)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\Gamma,\\Delta\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\n\\bigl((\\Gamma\\vdash\\varphi\\land\\forall\\psi\\in\\Gamma\\;(\\Delta\\vdash\\psi))\n\\to\\Delta\\vdash\\varphi\\bigr)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}tarski}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash)\\to\\Bigl[{}&amp;\n\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\Gamma\\;(\\Gamma\\vdash\\varphi)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq\\Delta\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\n(\\Gamma\\vdash\\varphi\\to\\Delta\\vdash\\varphi)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall\\Gamma,\\Delta\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\n\\bigl((\\Gamma\\vdash\\varphi\\land\\forall\\psi\\in\\Gamma\\;(\\Delta\\vdash\\psi))\n\\to\\Delta\\vdash\\varphi\\bigr)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>Tarski's axioms characterize consequence as a relation satisfying: (1) reflexivity — a set of formulas entails each of its members; (2) monotonicity — expanding the premise set preserves entailment; (3) transitivity — if a formula follows from a set, and each member of that set follows from another set, then the formula follows from the latter set.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"93-df-consequence","status":"resolved","id":"afd7605d365be7b6","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-consequence]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-logic","status":"resolved","id":"bd7e4207897c8db3","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-logic]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-language","status":"resolved","id":"a33dcee0f62c9026","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-language]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"c2ca1af9af149e69","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[93-df-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"93-df-logic","status":"resolved","id":"bd7e4207897c8db3","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$F$ is a formula carrier, $\\tau$ is its connective type, and $\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash)$ is the type-indexed logic predicate of [[93-df-logic]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"F","display":false},{"tex":"\\tau","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash)","display":false},{"tex":"\\Gamma,\\Delta\\subseteq F","display":false},{"tex":"\\varphi\\in F","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{ax\\text{-}tarski}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{Logic}_{\\tau}(F,\\vdash)\\to\\Bigl[{}&\n\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in\\Gamma\\;(\\Gamma\\vdash\\varphi)\\\\\n&\\land\\forall\\Gamma\\subseteq\\Delta\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\n(\\Gamma\\vdash\\varphi\\to\\Delta\\vdash\\varphi)\\\\\n&\\land\\forall\\Gamma,\\Delta\\subseteq F\\;\\forall\\varphi\\in F\\;\n\\bigl((\\Gamma\\vdash\\varphi\\land\\forall\\psi\\in\\Gamma\\;(\\Delta\\vdash\\psi))\n\\to\\Delta\\vdash\\varphi\\bigr)\\Bigr].\n\\end{aligned}"